): `malformed_none`, `soundness`, `vertex_coverage`, `edge_ordering`, `reachability_ordering`, `completeness`, `empty_graph`, `forward_dag`, `edgeless_graph`, `cycle_none`, `self_loop_none`, `two_cycle_none`, `unique_vertex_count`, `index_bijection`, and `first_permutation`.\n   - `Post_prop`, `topological_sort_post`, and `topological_sort_correct : Pre graph → Post_prop graph`.\n\n4. **Imperative Implementation & Equivalence Proofs** ([topological_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/topological_sort.lean#L737-L892)):\n   - Imperative implementations `pre_imp`, `is_topological_order_imp`, and `topological_sort_imp` using `Id.run do` with mutable state and loops.\n   - Proven equivalence theorems `pre_equiv`, `is_topological_order_equiv`, and `topological_sort_equiv`."}
